# Concurrent Gradle

Never run two full Gradle builds that share the same output dirs — they contend on `build/` and project `.gradle` (especially painful on Windows).

## desktop:debug + tests (same checkout)

`:desktop:debug` redirects all module outputs to `build-debug/` and the project cache to `.gradle-debug/` (see root `settings.gradle` / `build.gradle`). Default `build/` stays free for `:core:test` and other agent builds.

**Do not wait or stop the game** when status is BUSY from `:desktop:debug` — run tests in this same tree. Do not create a worktree only for that case.

## Before a long run

```bash
./gradlew --status
```

Idle daemons are fine to share across different checkouts.

## When BUSY for another reason

**Short one-shot BUSY** (another `:core:test` / compile that will finish soon): wait and poll until `IDLE`, then run. Do not report blocked or skip tests.

**Two long jobs that both use default `build/`** (e.g. `:desktop:run` if added later without a slot, or two test runs): use a **git worktree**, or wait. Do not start a second `./gradlew` that writes the same `build/`.

```bash
git worktree add ../iatdb-<purpose> <branch>
cd ../iatdb-<purpose>
./gradlew :core:test
```

Windows: `gradlew.bat`.

Other sessions may modify the same tree: at the end of a task, report only the files you changed; say plainly if other diffs came from elsewhere.

## Do not

- Start a second `./gradlew` in the same tree while another build writing **the same** `build/` (or same cache) is in progress
- Kill `:desktop:debug` just so agent tests can run
- Rely on `--project-cache-dir` alone without also splitting `build/` — incomplete isolation
- Use a separate `GRADLE_USER_HOME` unless you need daemon isolation (duplicates caches)

`org.gradle.parallel=true` only parallelizes tasks **inside one build**, not multiple CLI runs.
